---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { releaseSource } from "../data/navigation";
---

<Docs
  title="Configuration"
  description="Choose where client definitions live, how projects are enrolled, and which settings an operator or application owns."
  toc={[
    ["project", "Set up a project"],
    ["sources", "Manifest precedence"],
    ["consumer", "App-owned manifests"],
    ["environment", "Environment and authentication"],
    ["container", "Containers and migration"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="project">Set up a project</h2>
  <p>
    Use the Python interpreter where you installed Clink to generate
    project-local manifests, prompt files and an MCP registration. With a uv
    tool installation on POSIX, the following looks up that interpreter under
    the uv tools directory. Replace the project path with an existing checkout.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · project setup"
    code={
      '"$(uv tool dir)/clink-cli/bin/python" -m clink.setup --project /absolute/path/to/your-project --cli codex --cli claude'
    }
  />
  <p>
    Omit the repeated <code>--cli</code> flags to generate all bundled clients.
    Inside the project, <code>.clink/cli_clients/</code> holds definitions and{" "}
    <code>.clink/prompts/</code> holds their role prompts.{" "}
    <code>.mcp.json</code> binds the server to the project with machine-specific
    absolute paths. Setup reports conflicts with existing custom files. After a
    move, update the registration and reconnect.
  </p>
  <p>
    The source checkout also offers the session-local <code>/clink:setup</code>{" "}
    Claude Code plugin. Launch Claude Code with{" "}
    <code>--plugin-dir /absolute/path/to/clink-cli/integrations/claude</code> to
    enable it.{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/project-setup.md"}>Project setup details</a>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="sources">Manifest precedence</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Bundled client definitions</li>
    <li>
      Legacy <code>~/.pal/cli_clients/</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      User <code>~/.clink/cli_clients/</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      Explicitly bound project <code>.clink/cli_clients/</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>CLI_CLIENTS_CONFIG_PATH</code>, a JSON file or a directory
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A later entry replaces the entire case-insensitive client, including roles.
    Start with a generated complete manifest. <code>working_dir</code> must fall
    inside <code>allowed_roots</code>. Relative paths resolve against the
    manifest. Generated project definitions use <code>../..</code> to refer to
    their repository. Invalid snapshots stop startup. Restart after edits to
    manifest or role text.
  </p>
  <p>
    Programmatic generation loads its operator configuration independently of a
    request’s project path. Give the generation client its own explicit root
    with <a href="/cli/#allow">clink allow</a>. Native CLI login and project
    trust remain under the CLI’s control.
  </p>
  <h2 id="consumer">App-owned manifests</h2>
  <p>
    For a dedicated generation client, create an existing absolute configuration
    directory and place a family-named JSON file directly inside. Use the actual
    absolute executable path and canonical absolute roots. The following is a
    complete consumer manifest for Codex. With an empty list, enroll a directory
    explicitly before launch.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="codex.json · consumer configuration"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        schema_version: 1,
        name: "codex",
        adapter: "codex",
        command: "/absolute/path/to/codex",
        allowed_roots: [],
        generation_native: { inherit_env: [], required_env: [] },
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <Code
    label="Terminal · grant and generate with the same binding"
    code={
      "clink --consumer-config-dir /absolute/canonical/app-config allow /absolute/path/to/your-project --cli codex --yes --json\nclink --consumer-config-dir /absolute/canonical/app-config generate --request-json - < request.json"
    }
  />
  <p>
    Consumer bindings load only the selected directory. Normal project
    selection, user manifests and <code>CLI_CLIENTS_CONFIG_PATH</code> do not
    contribute to that configuration. Use one quoted executable path with no
    extra arguments. Keep credential values outside the manifest.{" "}
    <a
      href={
        releaseSource +
        "docs/cli-configuration.md#application-owned-generation-configuration"
      }
    >
      Consumer contract
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <h2 id="environment">Environment and authentication</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>
      <code>CLINK_DEFAULT_CLI</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Default consultation client, normally codex. Native task start requires
      its own explicit agent selection.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>CLINK_MAX_CONCURRENT</code>, <code>DISABLED_TOOLS</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Control the per-process pool and the comma-separated set of disabled MCP
      tools. Local version and client discovery stay available.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>CONVERSATION_TIMEOUT_HOURS</code>,{" "}
      <code>MAX_CONVERSATION_TURNS</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Control in-memory consultation retention. Saving a thread ID alone cannot
      recover it after restart.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>LOG_LEVEL</code>, <code>LOCALE</code>,{" "}
      <code>MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Configure logging, language guidance and the bounded MCP response budget.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Sign in through the agent’s own CLI. Native profiles can name specific extra
    environment variables with <code>inherit_env</code>. Every{" "}
    <code>required_env</code> name must also be inherited. See the{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + ".env.example"}>release environment template</a>{" "}
    and{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/cli-configuration.md"}>
      complete manifest guide
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <h2 id="container">Containers and migration</h2>
  <p>
    The supplied Compose setup runs provider-free discovery and local MCP tools
    with networking disabled. Build from the release source checkout, then let
    your MCP host own the attached stdio session.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · source checkout"
    code={
      "docker compose build clink-mcp\ndocker compose run --rm --no-deps -T clink-mcp"
    }
  />
  <p>
    The base image contains no logged-in CLI agents. For earlier PAL or wheel
    installations, check tool paths, full manifest replacement and native model
    names before moving registrations.{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docker/README.md"}>Container setup</a> ·{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/migration.md"}>Migration guide</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
